%% Bunny OS Phase 1 — Diagram 9 (file 14): Memory Retrieval and Update
%% Scoped retrieval, provenance, model use, verification, and write-back.
%% Two invariants: retrieval is scope-bounded by the Memory Service (not by the
%% model's request), and NOTHING writes durable memory silently (C8).

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant SH as Bunny Shell
    participant PE as Plan Engine
    participant MEM as Memory Service
    participant POL as Policy Engine
    participant CR as Capability Router
    participant M as Model
    participant AUD as Audit Service

    rect rgb(40, 48, 58)
    Note over PE,AUD: RETRIEVAL — scope is enforced by Bunny, not requested by the model
    PE->>MEM: retrieve for plan P in workspace W
    MEM->>MEM: filter by scope — workspace W only
    MEM->>MEM: exclude sensitive classes from provider context
    MEM->>MEM: rank by relevance × confidence × freshness
    MEM->>MEM: contradiction check against newer evidence
    MEM-->>PE: 4 records, each with provenance,<br/>valid-time, ingestion-time, confidence
    Note over MEM: a record without provenance is unstorable,<br/>so every returned record has one
    MEM->>AUD: retrieval record — what was returned, to what

    PE->>CR: compose request with retrieved context
    CR->>M: minimized context
    M-->>CR: response
    Note over CR,M: response is untrusted —<br/>it may propose a memory, never write one
    end

    rect rgb(40, 48, 58)
    Note over SH,U: VISIBLE USE — C8 principle 4
    PE->>SH: response + "drew on 2 memories"
    SH->>U: shows which records were used
    U->>SH: "that one is outdated"
    SH->>MEM: correct in flow
    MEM->>MEM: supersede record, keep prior version,<br/>set valid-time end
    MEM->>AUD: correction record
    Note over MEM: correction is one action at the moment<br/>of use, not a settings expedition
    end

    rect rgb(40, 48, 58)
    Note over PE,AUD: WRITE-BACK — proposals only
    PE->>MEM: propose candidate memories from completed plan
    MEM->>POL: memory write is a privileged action
    POL-->>MEM: requires attribution + user confirmation
    MEM->>SH: "Bunny noticed you prefer tabs<br/>(from today's session, workspace api-server)"
    SH->>U: keep / edit / forget
    U->>SH: keep
    SH->>MEM: confirmed
    MEM->>MEM: write with provenance, writer identity,<br/>scope = workspace, lineage to source
    MEM->>AUD: memory write — what wrote this, from what source, when
    end

    rect rgb(58, 34, 34)
    Note over MEM,AUD: DELETION CASCADE — designed in, never retrofitted
    U->>SH: delete this source
    SH->>MEM: delete
    MEM->>MEM: walk derivation lineage
    MEM->>MEM: remove derived summaries, embeddings, artifacts
    MEM->>AUD: deletion record with cascade manifest
    Note over MEM: retrofitted deletion in stateful AI systems<br/>is an unsolved mess — the lineage exists<br/>from record one for exactly this reason
    end
